Subject: [M152] Check for GL driver errors before marking SharedImage cleared
 in RasterDecoder

Original change's description:
> Check for GL driver errors before marking SharedImage cleared in RasterDecoder
>
> In Ganesh-GL, Skia's texture upload path does not check glGetError()
> and may report success even when an underlying GL driver
> under memory pressure drops texture uploads and latches GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY.
> If an uncleared SharedImage is uploaded under these conditions, it could
> be falsely marked cleared and subsequently read back, exposing
> uninitialized texture memory.
>
> This CL:
> 1. Adds DrainGLErrors(gl::GLApi* gl_api) to gpu/command_buffer/service/gl_utils.h
>    to drain driver error queues and return the first encountered error.
> 2. Drains and verifies GL driver errors before marking the destination
>    SharedImage cleared in both DoWritePixelsINTERNAL and WritePixelsYUV
>    when running on Ganesh-GL without context loss. If a GL error occurs,
>    the upload fails and the SharedImage remains uncleared.
>
